        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"The current implementation of `mx.random.normal` can produce `-inf` or `inf` values when the caller requests a half‑precision floating‑point dtype (`mx.float16` or `mx.bfloat16`). The test suite verifies that, for a large sample (shape=(10000,)), the absolute value of every element must be less than `mx.inf`. Your solution must modify the normal random number generator so that, for these half‑precision dtypes, no element of the returned array is infinite. The function must continue to accept the same parameters (shape, loc, scale, dtype, etc.) and return an array of the requested dtype. All other dtypes (e.g., `mx.float32`, `mx.float64`) must retain their existing behavior, and the overall reproducibility of the generator should not be adversely affected beyond eliminating the infinite values. The implementation should be observable only through the public API; the test checks that `mx.all(a < mx.inf)` evaluates to true for the half‑precision outputs.\"\n",
