        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nNow I understand the issue. The `normal` function uses `erfinv` which can produce very large values when the input is close to ±1. For half-precision types, the maximum finite values are much smaller than for float32:\n- float16 max: ~65504\n- bfloat16 max: ~3.4e38\n- float32 max: ~3.4e38\n\nThe issue is that when sampling from the normal distribution, extreme values (several standard deviations from the mean) can overflow to infinity in half-precision.\n\nThe solution is to clip the output values to a safe range that prevents infinity. Let me look at what values would cause issues:\n\n",
          "time": {
            "start": 1782376392742,
            "end": 1782376392791
          },
          "id": "prt_efde96826001KbqR5Z2Nh4YehE",
          "sessionID": "ses_102171855ffeCfDQ6qEIS2IpME",
          "messageID": "msg_efde94323001L4NfnWOi1SVpnO"
        },
        {
          "type": "tool",
          "tool": "bash",
          "callID": "call_4f0a9704edc24321b533b254",
          "state": {
            "status": "completed",
            "input": {
              "command": "python3 -c \"\nimport mlx.core as mx\nimport math\n\n# Check max values for different dtypes\nprint('float16 max:', mx.finfo(mx.float16).max)\nprint('bfloat16 max:', mx.finfo(mx.bfloat16).max)\nprint('float32 max:', mx.finfo(mx.float32).max)\n\n# Check what erfinv values would cause overflow\n# normal = sqrt(2) * erfinv(x)\n# For float16: erfinv(x) must be < 65504 / sqrt(2) ≈ 46319\n# But erfinv approaches infinity as x approaches 1, so we need to clip\n\n# Let's see what input to erfinv would give us the max value\n# erfinv(x) = max / sqrt(2)\n# x = erf(max / sqrt(2))\n\nsqrt2 = math.sqrt(2)\nfloat16_max = mx.finfo(mx.float16).max.item()\nbfloat16_max = mx.finfo(mx.bfloat16).max.item()\n\nprint()\nprint('float16 max / sqrt(2):', float16_max / sqrt2)\nprint('bfloat16 max / sqrt(2):', bfloat16_max / sqrt2)\n\n# erf(46319) is essentially 1.0, so we need to clip the erfinv output\n\"\n",
              "description": "Check float16 and bfloat16 max values"
            },
