        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nI've confirmed the issue - `mx.random.normal` with `float16` can produce `-inf` values. Now let me understand the solution better. The problem is that the Box-Muller transform via `erfinv` can produce very large values that overflow in half-precision.\n\nThe solution is to clip the output of the normal distribution to a safe maximum value for half-precision types. Let me look at what a reasonable clip value would be:\n\n",
