          "text": "\n\nNow I understand the issue better. The `normal` function uses `uniform` to generate values in the range `(-1, 1)` (specifically using `std::nextafter(-1.0f, 0.0f)` to `1.0f`), and then applies `erfinv` which can produce very large values when the input is close to ±1.\n\nThe solution is to clip the final output of the normal distribution to the maximum finite value for the dtype. Let me implement this:\n\n",
